{#
    Hero slider — merchant-placeable home component.
    | Variable                       | Type     | Description                              |
    | component.slides[].image        | string   | image URL (wide, ~1400×580)              |
    | component.slides[].image_mobile | ?string  | square image, shown under 768px          |
    | component.slides[].video        | ?string  | background clip; the image is its poster |
    | component.slides[].video_mobile | ?string  | phone file for the clip                  |
    | component.slides[].title        | ?string  | localized server-side                    |
    | component.slides[].description | ?string  | localized server-side                    |
    | component.slides[].button_text | ?string  | CTA label, localized server-side         |
    | component.slides[].button_url   | ?string  | CTA target                               |
    | position                        | int      | render order index, starts at 0          |

    Mobile media: each viewport prefers its own uploads — video first, then
    image — and falls back to the other viewport's media only when it has none
    of its own. So a mobile-only video plays on phones while desktop keeps the
    still, and vice versa. When the two viewports want different element kinds
    (one a video, one an image) both are rendered and a media query shows one
    at a time via the --desktop-only / --mobile-only classes. The image swap is
    a <picture> source, so the browser picks it before paint and re-evaluates
    on resize; the video swap lives in home.js because `src` has to be chosen
    once, off the data-hero-src / data-hero-src-mobile attributes. "Phone"
    is max-width 767px in all three places (source, CSS, JS).

    Customizer bindings — full rules in README, "Customizer annotations".
    | Element             | Tag                                             |
    | .hero-slider__slide | data-falak-field="slides" data-falak-bind="none" |

    `slides` is a collection, so its value is a list rather than a string.
    bind="none" keeps it selectable in the preview while leaving the editing to
    the panel; without it the customizer would write the whole list into the
    slide as text the first time the merchant touched that field.

    Styleable parts — every slide shares one rule, so styling the title styles
    all of them, which is what "the slide titles" means.
    | slide_content | .hero-slider__content |
    | slide_title   | each slide's h2       |
    | slide_text    | each slide's p        |
    | slide_button  | each slide's a.btn    |
#}
{% set show_arrows = component.show_arrows is defined ? component.show_arrows : true %}
{% set show_dots = component.show_dots is defined ? component.show_dots : true %}
{% set autoplay = component.autoplay is defined ? component.autoplay : true %}

<section class="block block--hero-slider" id="hero-slider-{{ position }}" {{ falak_section() }}>
    {#
        The slider's JS reads its behaviour off these attributes rather than
        hard-coding it, so a merchant can stop the carousel or slow it down.
        A speed of 0 is how "do not advance" reaches the script.
    #}
    <div class="hero-slider"
         data-autoplay="{{ autoplay ? (component.autoplay_speed|default('5000')) : '0' }}">
        {% for slide in component.slides %}
            {#
                What each viewport plays: its own video if uploaded,
                otherwise its own image, otherwise the other viewport's
                media. `video_desktop` / `video_mobile` end up holding the
                file that viewport should PLAY — empty means that viewport
                shows an image instead.

                Only a URL counts as a video. The fields are free text in
                the customizer, and a stray word there would turn the slide
                into a <video> that 404s, with the image cropped as its
                poster instead of shown as the picture.
            #}
            {% set image_mobile = slide.image_mobile|default('')|trim %}
            {% set video_desktop = slide.video|default('')|trim %}
            {% set video_mobile = slide.video_mobile|default('')|trim %}
            {% if not (video_desktop starts with 'http' or video_desktop starts with '/') %}{% set video_desktop = '' %}{% endif %}
            {% if not (video_mobile starts with 'http' or video_mobile starts with '/') %}{% set video_mobile = '' %}{% endif %}
            {# Whether the merchant uploaded anything for phones at all: that
               is what turns the phone slide into a square (see app.css),
               before the fallbacks below borrow the desktop media. #}
            {% set has_mobile_media = image_mobile or video_mobile %}
            {% if not video_mobile and not image_mobile %}
                {% set video_mobile = video_desktop %}
            {% endif %}
            {% if not video_desktop and not slide.image %}
                {% set video_desktop = video_mobile %}
            {% endif %}
            <div class="hero-slider__slide{{ loop.first ? ' is-active' : '' }}{{ has_mobile_media ? ' hero-slider__slide--mobile-media' : '' }}" data-falak-field="slides" data-falak-label="{{ trans('editor.field.slides') }}" data-falak-bind="none">
                {% if video_desktop or video_mobile %}
                    {#
                        A background clip. Muted + playsinline is what lets it
                        autoplay at all; the slide image is its poster, so the
                        slide never flashes empty and a browser that refuses to
                        play still shows the merchant's picture. No `src` in the
                        markup: home.js picks the phone or desktop file (and the
                        phone poster) once, off the data-hero-* attributes, then
                        plays only the visible slide's clip — and leaves every
                        clip on its poster under reduced motion. A viewport with
                        no data-hero-src of its own shows the <picture> instead.
                        Decorative, so hidden from assistive tech.
                    #}
                    <video class="hero-slider__video{{ not video_mobile ? ' hero-slider__video--desktop-only' : '' }}{{ not video_desktop ? ' hero-slider__video--mobile-only' : '' }}"
                           data-hero-video
                           {% if video_desktop %}data-hero-src="{{ video_desktop }}"{% endif %}
                           {% if video_mobile %}data-hero-src-mobile="{{ video_mobile }}"{% endif %}
                           {% if slide.image %}poster="{{ slide.image }}"{% endif %}
                           {% if image_mobile %}data-hero-poster-mobile="{{ image_mobile }}"{% endif %}
                           muted loop playsinline aria-hidden="true"
                           preload="{{ loop.first ? 'auto' : 'none' }}"></video>
                {% endif %}
                {% if not video_desktop or not video_mobile %}
                    <picture class="hero-slider__picture{{ video_desktop ? ' hero-slider__picture--mobile-only' : '' }}{{ video_mobile ? ' hero-slider__picture--desktop-only' : '' }}">
                        {% if image_mobile and not video_mobile %}
                            <source media="(max-width: 767px)" srcset="{{ image_mobile }}">
                        {% endif %}
                        <img class="hero-slider__img" src="{{ slide.image|default(image_mobile) }}"
                             alt="{{ slide.title|default('') }}"{{ loop.first ? '' : ' loading="lazy"' }}>
                    </picture>
                {% endif %}
                <div class="hero-slider__content container" data-falak-part="slide_content">
                    {% if slide.title %}<h2 data-falak-part="slide_title">{{ slide.title }}</h2>{% endif %}
                    {% if slide.description %}<p data-falak-part="slide_text">{{ slide.description }}</p>{% endif %}
                    {% if slide.button_text|default(null) and slide.button_url|default(null) %}
                        <a class="btn btn--primary" data-falak-part="slide_button" href="{{ slide.button_url }}">{{ slide.button_text }}</a>
                    {% endif %}
                </div>
            </div>
        {% endfor %}

        {% if component.slides|length > 1 and show_arrows %}
            <button type="button" class="hero-slider__arrow hero-slider__arrow--prev"
                    data-slide-dir="-1" aria-label="{{ trans('common.previous') }}"><span>‹</span></button>
            <button type="button" class="hero-slider__arrow hero-slider__arrow--next"
                    data-slide-dir="1" aria-label="{{ trans('common.next') }}"><span>›</span></button>

        {% endif %}

        {% if component.slides|length > 1 and show_dots %}
            <div class="hero-slider__dots" role="tablist">
                {% for slide in component.slides %}
                    <button type="button"
                            class="hero-slider__dot{{ loop.first ? ' is-active' : '' }}"
                            data-slide-to="{{ loop.index0 }}"
                            aria-label="{{ loop.index }}"></button>
                {% endfor %}
            </div>
        {% endif %}
    </div>
</section>
